content.text:
Yes—correct. I found no demonstrated production-logic bug in the PR.

The implementation correctly:

- applies one shared deadline to the batch;
- stops starting checkpoint writes after expiry;
- records degradation;
- clears pending IDs under the existing best-effort contract;
- selects the intended agent-specific budgets.

The failure is in the test’s timing assumption. It expects a 25 ms deadline path to complete within 40 ms, but race instrumentation adds enough preprocessing overhead to exceed that threshold even though cancellation behaves correctly.

So I’d characterize it as:

- Production logic: looks correct.
- Test: flaky/incompatible with required `-race` execution.
- Merge status: still worth fixing before merge because it can fail CI.
- Severity: Medium is more proportionate than High; “request changes” only because the repository requires race-enabled tests to pass reliably.

